{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>It is tzara'at.</b> Meaning: even what the priest had already declared pure upon it is now, retroactively, revealed to be impure — for a pure mispachat does not spread at all. And Scripture informs us in this declaration to say that the spreading need not be as large as the measure of the nega; rather, any amount whatsoever — for we render judgment concerning the mispachat itself that it is tzara'at. Understand this."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:47.842919477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}